A||N||8||KRMFiero||Turbo's, Nitrous, performance parts||||1||
Z||000000||KRMFiero||10-04-2000||06:37 PM||||I have a 84 Fiero with a 4 cylinder automatic in it, does anyone know of any Nitrous kits that would fit on easy, or any turbos that i could pull out of junkyard cars cheap or anyother performance parts to make my little 4 cylinder go faster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> I really would want to put a turbo in it or Nitrous well anyways, anyone have any Ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||10-04-2000||07:02 PM||||speaking from the past go with a used T-3 turbo and not NOS. NOS is cheaper but is much harder in the duke than a smoth turbo. I have been toying with the Idea of re-working the stock A/C bracket to take teh RSM supercharger  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> but @ $3000 i din't feel like messing it up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> you can get a turbo off a late 80's T-bird. or for more boost a 95-99 Eclipse T3/T4 hybird. a stock 2.5 WILL NOT take more than 10 PSI EVER. when the boost gauge hits 10 that knock that you hear wont go away  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I had a turbo on my first Fiero (84 SE Auto) i got it for $3500 from a dodge dealer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> the system  w/ 558k miles on it. The turbo was poorly instaled they used an adapter the mount the turbo, it had a cheap waste gate and no blow off valve. I could put together a system similar to that with a flanged Manifold & a blow-off valve for around $400-800 less the turbo & wastegate. E mail me if you want more info. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||baldlobo||10-04-2000||07:31 PM||||So what does everyone think of putting a Vortec supercharger with 3-5 PSI of boost on a Iron Duke?<p>[This message has been edited by baldlobo (edited 10-04-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000003||KRMFiero||10-04-2000||07:38 PM||||hmmm I think i will look for a turbo...... well a vortec supercharger - I dont think that would be possibly to put on (i doubt the make one for a 2.5) if it is possible it will take alot of time..<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||10-04-2000||08:51 PM||||a T-28 or a T-03 from <A HREF="http://www.turbonetics.com" TARGET=_blank>www.turbonetics.com</A>  will work ok for 8-10 psi. and a lot cheaper than a hybrid unit. toss on an MSD 6BTM and you'll be fine. do it all day on 10-15 year old hondas. <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  nitrous is nice and cheap.. but it runs out at the worst times... been there... <A HREF="http://www.nitrouexpress.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrouexpress.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.nitrousworks.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrousworks.com</A>  the stuff from NOS is nice but not the best fuel delivery system. <A HREF="http://www.nosnitrous.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nosnitrous.com</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Xtreme Fiero's||10-04-2000||09:01 PM||||<BR>1FST2M6: Where can I find a diagram of the mouning flange for a T-28, T-03 or T-3 turbos. I would like to sell turbo kits/ manifolds but I cant go out & buy 50 diffrent turbo units. where should I start?||||reg||1
Z||000006||BroCar 87||10-04-2000||09:06 PM||||Hey Xtreme, don't you have a website? I think I came across it once. Are you making a 4-2-1 header for the 2.5, or a TRUE dual exhaust?? I THOUGHT it was yours but sorry if I was wrong. Well whoever it is, I love the ideas they had. If was yours can you tell more about them!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR>AGAIN sorry if its not you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg"> <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||6
Z||000007||Sillhouette.com||10-04-2000||09:23 PM||||I don't think vortech makes supercharger with such low output.  It's never a problem to bleed excess pressure away.  I think you should do it.  You'd probably be quite unique and suprising on the road.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000008||baldlobo||10-04-2000||10:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sillhouette.com:<BR><B>I don't think vortech makes supercharger with such low output.  It's never a problem to bleed excess pressure away.  I think you should do it.  You'd probably be quite unique and suprising on the road.  <P>Later</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the lowest psi is 10 on the vortech site, so all you have to do is change the pully to one that is bigger in diamiter(ok so I don't have a dictionary with me). oh yeah it's the V-1 A trim supercharger.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
